  "finalMessage": "Porto Notes is implemented and passing the smoke test.\n\nSummary of what was built:\n- **`src/main.ts`** — app logic: loads/seeds notes from `localStorage` (falling back to `src/fixtures.json` on first run), renders the feed newest-first, wires the form/search/click handlers, and syncs selection + query to the URL fragment (`#q=...&note=...`) via `history.replaceState`, restoring on load and `hashchange`.\n- **`src/richtext.ts`** — a whitelist-based sanitizer: parses body text with `DOMParser` and rebuilds only `<b>`, `<strong>`, `<i>`, `<em>`, `<a href>` (protocol-checked, `rel=noopener noreferrer`), and `<br>` (plus bare `\\n` → `<br>`), dropping everything else (verified `<script>`/`onerror` payloads don't execute and don't survive in the DOM). Titles render as plain text since they come from a plain `<input>`.\n- **`index.html`** — accessible form/labels matching the required element contract (`#note-form`, `#title`, `#body`, `#avatar`, `#search`, `#results-line`, `#feed`).\n- **`src/style.css`** — minimal accessible styling with visible focus states.\n- **`src/fixtures.json`** — copied from the seed data.\n\nVerified end-to-end in a headless browser: seed rendering, adding notes (rich text + avatar), search filtering with `results for \"...\"`, click-to-select with `aria-current`, and full state restoration from the URL fragment after reload.",
